WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.202
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:06.002 --> 00:00:07.870
Give me one minute and I'll show you

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:09.460
how Data Catalog can empower you

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:14.076
to better discover, understand,
and manage all of your data assets.

00:00:14.076 --> 00:00:16.642
Data Catalog
is Google Cloud's highly scalable

00:00:16.642 --> 00:00:19.405
data discovery and metadata
management service.

00:00:19.405 --> 00:00:22.351
Data Catalog provides you
with a simple-to-use search interface

00:00:22.351 --> 00:00:25.981
for data discovery and an API
for programmatic access

00:00:25.981 --> 00:00:27.884
and building custom applications.

00:00:27.884 --> 00:00:30.341
It's powered by the same
Google search technology

00:00:30.341 --> 00:00:34.084
that supports popular Google services
like Drive and Gmail.

00:00:34.084 --> 00:00:36.482
And it's fully managed
for effortless setup

00:00:36.482 --> 00:00:38.723
with no additional
infrastructure to manage.

00:00:39.364 --> 00:00:41.875
With Data Catalog,
you create tag templates

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:45.009
that let you tag your data assets
with structured tags.

00:00:45.009 --> 00:00:48.381
Structured tags let you capture
any complex business metadata,

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.798
like the person responsible
for that data asset,

00:00:50.798 --> 00:00:53.624
data classification, retention policies,

00:00:53.624 --> 00:00:55.823
or whether the data contains sensitive,

00:00:55.823 --> 00:00:58.056
personal, identifiable information.

00:00:58.056 --> 00:00:59.193
Speaking of PII,

00:00:59.193 --> 00:01:02.663
Data Catalog has built-in
Cloud Data Loss Prevention integration

00:01:02.663 --> 00:01:06.253
so that it can detect and tag
your sensitive data automatically.

00:01:06.253 --> 00:01:09.827
Do your data assets exist across
a lot of different systems?

00:01:09.827 --> 00:01:12.966
Data Catalog not only supports
Google Cloud data sources,

00:01:12.966 --> 00:01:16.556
but also third-party ones
via open-source connectors.

00:01:16.556 --> 00:01:17.906
With these integrations,

00:01:17.906 --> 00:01:20.092
you'll be able to search
all your business metadata

00:01:20.092 --> 00:01:21.860
and receive one unified view

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.800
no matter where your data resides.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.904
Next time you're looking for a way
to manage all of your data assets,

00:01:26.904 --> 00:01:29.109
take a minute and check out Data Catalog.

00:01:29.109 --> 00:01:32.635
Find out more
at <i>cloud.google.com/data-catalog</i>

00:01:32.635 --> 00:01:35.508
♪ [music] ♪

